# TODO - Owner-controlled Wi-Fi Bluetooth and AirDrop acceptance

## Objective

Only AFTER every P0-P4 record is source-complete and the indefinite hardening
hold is expressly ended by the owner, begin the real Dell diagnostic/repair
loop in this ChatGPT conversation.

When this is the ONLY open TODO, the exact main commit must have complete,
integrated AR9565 source and no known source-resolvable blockers. The owner
can then request its first compilation through ONE specifically authorized
GitHub `build-v*` tag. No tag, build or experiment is authorized by reaching
this state. Local builds and alternate CI triggers are not permitted.

The acceptance objective is fully functional native Wi-Fi on the specified
Dell/Tahoe target, plus the requested Bluetooth/coexistence and AirDrop
behavior. Treat 100% functionality as the required outcome, never as an
unobserved result or a promise that static review proves first-run success.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Owner explicitly ends the hold and separately authorizes each build,
      install and hardware experiment.
- [ ] Compile only the reviewed commit via the single explicitly approved
      GitHub build tag; record the artifact hash and actual build diagnostics.
- [ ] Observe OpenCore injection without unresolved imports/relocations,
      Tahoe boot and physical 168c:0036 identity with supported true SREV.
- [ ] Owner tests native Wi-Fi, WPA2/CCMP encrypted IP, recovery, sleep and RF safety.
- [ ] Observe 2.4 GHz scanning, actual WPA2 association, DHCP/DNS/TCP traffic,
      reconnect after sleep, legal transmit-power constraints and no kernel
      panic during the owner-authorized runs; record limits and failures.
- [ ] Identify and verify Bluetooth hardware and coexistence separately.
- [ ] Demonstrate AirDrop discovery and bidirectional transfer with compatible Apple devices.
- [ ] Owner posts actual results here; agents coordinate code fixes in their chat
      and commit directly to main, iterating only with new owner permission.
- [ ] Record real logs/results and remaining limits, never equating theory with success.
- [ ] Owner explicitly requests closing THIS TODO. Neither successful checks
      nor permission to compile, install or test authorizes closure.

## Standing instruction while open

This record MUST NOT be closed, moved to completed or removed from TODO.md
without the owner's explicit request to close it. If it is the only open
record and no new owner instruction arrives, continue theoretical hardening
of the entire driver indefinitely using web research, upstream comparisons
and static reasoning. Repair evidence-backed panic, lifetime, concurrency,
DMA, power, security and regulatory defects; maintain provenance and reopen
source records when required work is found. Do not request early device
tests or infer authorization from elapsed time or source completeness.

